---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import profileImage from '@assets/images/profile.webp';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="max-width-56 width-100 margin-auto column flex gap-2">
    <span></span>
    <section class="gap grid justify-content-center text-align-center">
      <img
        src={profileImage.src}
        alt="Andrew Noblet profile photo"
        class="profile-image margin-auto"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <h1>Meet Andrew Noblet</h1>
      <p class="bold-5 max-width-56">
        Hello! I'm <strong>Andrew Noblet</strong>, a curious soul with a truly
        global perspective—born in Chile and shaped by experiences living in
        Puerto Rico, Ohio, and now New York. I'm passionate about exploring life
        through diverse interests that span the physical, creative, and
        intellectual. Drawing wisdom from Eastern philosophy, Greek mythology,
        and the simple joy of learning something new, I believe in living
        authentically and embracing the adventure that each day brings.
      </p>
    </section>
    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Personal Facts</h2>
      <ul class="column flex gap-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        <li><strong>Full Name:</strong> Andrew Noblet</li>
        <li><strong>Born in:</strong> Chile</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Life Journey:</strong> Chile → Puerto Rico → Ohio → <strong
            >New York</strong
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub:</strong>
          <a href="https://github.com/anoblet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >anoblet</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Philosophy:</strong> Eastern wisdom meets Western curiosity—always
          learning, always growing
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motto:</strong> "Less noise, more meaning"
        </li>
      </ul>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Hobbies & Passions</h2>
      <div class="column flex gap-1">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-size-1-125 margin-bottom-0-25">Physical & Outdoor</h3>
          <p class="font-size-1-125">
            Skateboarding (been at it since I was young enough to petition my
            town for a skatepark at 14!), snowboarding, and bike riding. There's
            something about the rhythm and flow of these activities that
            connects me to the moment and the environment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-size-1-125 margin-bottom-0-25">
            Creative & Technical
          </h3>
          <p class="font-size-1-125">
            Playing guitar, diving into 3D printing projects, and tinkering with
            smart home technology. I love the blend of creativity and technical
            problem-solving—whether it's learning a new song or printing
            something useful for the house.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-size-1-125 margin-bottom-0-25">
            Intellectual Pursuits
          </h3>
          <p class="font-size-1-125">
            Politics, history, Eastern philosophy (Confucianism, Buddhism,
            Shintoism), and Greek mythology. I'm fascinated by how ancient
            wisdom applies to modern life and how understanding the past helps
            navigate the present.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Life Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="margin-bottom-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        I find deep meaning in the balance and wisdom of Eastern philosophy.
        Confucian principles of harmony and continuous learning, Buddhist
        mindfulness and compassion, and Shinto reverence for nature all
        influence how I approach daily life.
      </p>
      <p class="font-size-1-125">
        The stories of Greek mythology remind me that human struggles and
        triumphs are timeless—we're all part of something larger, navigating
        similar challenges of growth, purpose, and connection. Minimalism in all
        things: less noise, more meaning.
      </p>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Early Adventures</h2>
      <p class="margin-bottom-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        My curiosity started young. At <strong>13</strong>, I built my first
        website at
        <strong>nebulae.org</strong> and dove into learning PHP with php-nuke. By
        <strong>14</strong>, I was passionate enough about skateboarding to
        petition my town to build a skatepark—and they did!
      </p>
      <p class="margin-bottom-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        I bought a several-hundred-page book on Adobe ColdFusion and read it
        cover-to-cover, used Adobe Dreamweaver religiously, and by my teens was
        building my own water-cooled computer. Let's just say I learned the
        importance of preparation the hard way—towels were definitely needed! 😅
      </p>
      <p class="font-size-1-125">
        These early adventures taught me that curiosity, persistence, and a
        willingness to learn from mistakes are the best tools for any journey.
      </p>
    </card-component>

    <card-component>
      <h2 class="font-size-1-25 margin-bottom-0-5">Life in New York</h2>
      <p class="margin-bottom-0-5 font-size-1-125">
        These days, I'm enjoying the energy and diversity of New York while
        staying connected to the simple pleasures. Whether I'm exploring the
        city on my bike, working on a 3D printing project, or diving into a book
        about history or philosophy, I try to approach each day with curiosity
        and openness.
      </p>
      <p class="font-size-1-125">
        I love connecting with people who share similar passions—whether that's
        discussing the parallels between ancient Stoicism and modern minimalism,
        sharing skateboarding stories, or just appreciating good design and
        thoughtful solutions to everyday problems.
      </p>
    </card-component>

    <consultation-component class="margin-top-4"></consultation-component>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .profile-image {
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--tertiary-color);
    display: block;
    height: 50vw;
    max-height: 16rem;
    max-width: 16rem;
    object-fit: cover;
    position: relative;
    width: 50vw;
    z-index: 1;
  }
</style>
<script>
  import '@components/card';
  import '@components/consultation';
</script>
